    "updated_at": "2021-03-23T09:50:39Z",
    "body": "`<rp>` is only allowed as child of `<ruby>`. In this case the behavior is undefined. We had a discussion on the Unicode mailgroup and I actually like this idea. The problem is that the semantic part of `<sub>` and `<sup>` gets lost if you copy rendered HTML from your browser to an application which only knows plaintext. E. g. `2<sup>3</sup>` becomes `23`. The Unicode replacement characters like ³ are not sufficient, because they cannot cover nested super- and subscripts, for example.",
    "author_association": "NONE",
    "pin": null,
