    "created_at": "2021-03-23T13:30:27Z",
    "updated_at": "2021-03-23T13:30:27Z",
    "body": "I thought about the topic and see that reusing `<rp>` would break downwards-compatibility.  `<rp>`, `<noscript>` and the custom elements are specifically designed, with the thought in mind, that legacy browsers ignore unknown tags and treat them similar to `<span>`. Given that there is a browser which knows `<sup>`, but not `<rp>`, the expression `e<sup><rp>^(</rp>i&InvisibleTimes;&pi;<rp>)</rp></sup>` would be rendered e<sup>^(i&InvisibleTimes;&pi;)</sup> instead of e<sup>i&InvisibleTimes;&pi;</sup> or e^(i&InvisibleTimes;&pi;).",
    "author_association": "NONE",
    "pin": null,
